WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.767
-Our next guest is

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.367
a comedy legend who has

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.534
influenced generations
of comedians.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.901
You could see her
at the Throckmorton Theatre

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:10.868
in Mill Valley, California,
February 14th.

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:13.467
Making her 10th appearance
on "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:16.100
please welcome the very funny...

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.033
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:24.801
♪♪

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:26.968
[ Whistling ]
Thank you. Thank you!

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:28.267
Thank you so much.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:30.467
Thank you very much.
Thank you. So,

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.601
I guess you noticed
that I have gray hair.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.801
[ Laughter ]
Yes. And I like it.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.968
I really love it.
It's very low-maintenance.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:40.767
Plus, I've noticed that I get
a lot more looks from guys

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:41.868
now that my hair is gray.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.934
[ Laughter and cheering ]
Yes.

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:45.400
And I think I know why.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.067
I think it's because they think

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:49.267
I can't get pregnant.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:51.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.601
Guys like that.

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:54.901
Yeah.

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.000
Yeah. I'm not afraid to tell you
how old I am,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.534
but I'm going
to give you a clue.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:01.601
I actually said this
to my friends.

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:02.701
I was at my friend's apartment

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.701
and I actually said
to her, out loud,

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.100
"Boy, that's a nice pill caddy."

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:13.267
That's how old I am, yes.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.901
I had to get
a new pill caddy recently

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:17.167
because my doctor
gave me a new prescription

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.501
and I'm on so much medication
that I couldn't jam

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:21.200
one more pill
into the compartment.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.234
[ Laughter ]
So, I had to go to CVS,

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:25.501
to the pill caddies
and prosthetics aisle.

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:27.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.334
And I don't know
if you've shopped for this,

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:31.033
but there's a whole hierarchy
of pill caddies.

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:33.200
[ Laughter ]
You start with your
entry level pill caddy.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.467
It's the single-compartment
pill caddy.

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.701
Then you move
into the AM/PM pill caddy.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:38.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.133
Then the
AM/noon/evening pill caddy.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:44.701
[ Laughter ]
Then the AM/noon/evening/bedtime
pill caddy.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:47.167
[ Laughter ]
Then, basically,
you have to hire a caddy

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:48.167
to hand you your pills all day

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:49.534
[indistinct].

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:52.968
[ Cheering ]

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:55.667
Okay. Okay. Alright.

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.834
Here's how old I am, Really,
here's how old I am.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:00.968
I was walking my dog and we're
at the end of the block

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.400
and there was this kid,
about 11 years old,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.701
and he's riding his skateboard

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:06.601
and he's talking to his friend
on his speakerphone.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.033
And he says to his friend,

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.567
"I'm on the corner
of 18th and Oak."

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:13.767
And I hear his friend say,
through the phone to him,

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:16.000
"Are you near that old lady
with the dog?"

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:20.501
And I said,
"I'm not an old lady!

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.033
I'm not an old lady!"

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.801
Nobody's listening to me,
by the way. I'm just screaming.

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.901
[ Laughter ]
"I'm not an old lady!

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.567
[ Applause ]
Thereby proving I'm an old lady!

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:31.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.033
And I get these old-people
coupons, now.

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:35.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:37.000
I got a coupon recently

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.801
for ash burial at sea.

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:40.901
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:42.067
A coupon.

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:43.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:46.534
It said, "Ash burial at sea,
$595."

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:48.934
And on the bottom,
in smaller print, it said,

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.167
"Reduce the high cost of dying."

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:52.701
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:56.067
"Gee, I'd like to die,
but it's just so expensive.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:57.701
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:00.133
It there was a sale on dying,
I'd be dead right now."

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:06.467
So, I have a daughter.
She's 19.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:08.534
Very interesting age.

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:11.434
She hates me, so, she's right
on track developmentally.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.367
[ Laughter and applause ]
The only thing she likes to do

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:15.501
with me is go to Costco.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:17.601
And I love Costco.
A lot of people love Costco,

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:20.434
but I've realized that,
at this stage in my life,

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:22.767
it doesn't even make sense
for me to go there

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:24.300
because there's nothing
I can buy there

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.267
that I'll live to finish.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:27.334
[ Laughter and oohs ]

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:29.334
I can't use that many Q-tips.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.901
[ Laughter ]
Every time I'm there

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.267
with my daughter
and we're leaving,

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:33.934
I always point to the cart
and I look at her and I say,

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:35.601
"Someday,
this will all be yours.

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:37.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.133
This is my legacy."

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:42.200
[ Cheering ]

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.434
Yes, I've been on the planet
for a while,

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.100
ladies and gentlemen.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.901
I remember this song that I
learned in the third grade.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:51.734
You'll probably know this,
from the East Coast.

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:53.667
"The Erie Canal"?
You know the song?

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.501
I'll sing it for you.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.501
♪ I've got a mule
and her name is Sal ♪

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:00.734
♪ Fifteen miles
on the Erie Canal ♪

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:03.467
♪ She's a good old worker
and a good old pal ♪

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:05.734
♪ Fifteen miles
on the Erie Canal ♪

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:08.367
♪ She's hauled some barges
in our day ♪

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.767
♪ Filled with lumber,
coal, and hay ♪

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:13.100
[ Clapping rhythmically ]
♪ And she knows every
inch of the way ♪

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.434
♪ From Albany to Buffalo ♪

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.033
[ Laughter and cheering ]
Now, wait.

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:21.734
I have known that song
since the third grade.

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:24.734
It's been up here for 59 years.

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:27.601
And that is why,
when I go to the mall,

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:28.868
I can't find my car.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.567
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:04:31.567 --> 00:04:33.767
I'm in the parking ramp,
clicking my remote,

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:35.200
hoping I hear something.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.501
All I hear is a guy
one mile over, going --

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.901
♪ I've got a mule
and her name is Sal ♪

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:42.534
[ Laughter and applause ]
He can't find his car, either.

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:44.367
Thank you so much.
I'm Cathy Ladman.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.934
[ Cheering and applause ]
You were great.

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:47.100
Thanks.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.367
[ Whistling ]

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:49.033
-This is your --

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:51.834
This is --
This is your legacy.

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.200
[Indistinct]

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.100
Cathy Ladman!

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.067
I love you.

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:56.067
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:58.934
See Cathy at the
Throckmorton Theatre

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:01.868
in Mill Valley, California,
February 14th.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.000
We'll be right back.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.968
Number 10.
Number 10.

